  "sourceTitle": "Egg Yolk Cookies",
  "sourceText": "Egg Yolk Cookies\nBy: Carrie Barr\nPublished: Tuesday, December 15, 2009 - 1:41pm\n\nIngredients\n\n\n\n\n12 egg yolks\n1 cup brown sugar\n1 cup white sugar\n1 1/2 cups shortening\n2 teaspoons lemon or orange flavoring\n3 1/2 cups flour\n1/2 teaspoon salt\n1 teaspoon soda\n2 teaspoons baking powder\n\nPreparation\n\n1 Cream sugar with shortening. Add slightly beaten egg yolks.   2 Sift dry ingredients; add to creamed mixture. Add flavoring. 3 Roll in balls then in sugar and flatten out. Bake 7 to 10 minutes at 350 degrees.",
  "parsedSource": {
